 ## Delivery
 
 The [reminder implementation](../../larder/reminders.py) holds the timing, message and channel setting.
 
-## Why SMS
+## Previous email trial
 
 The April–June 2025 trial used email for pickup reminders. The provider reported that 34% of reminder emails were
 never opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders. Each missed pickup leaves a packed bag;
 its fresh food goes in the bin by closing time. Many members share one phone in the family and never check email,
 but they see SMS messages.
 
-SMS resumed on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups returned to 6% by August. Email would save the reported SMS cost
-of €40 a month, but the trial showed that this saving came with more missed pickups and food waste. The maintainer
-therefore confirmed that pickup reminders would keep using SMS in [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md).
+SMS resumed on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups returned to 6% by August. The maintainer previously confirmed
+that pickup reminders would keep using SMS. The current switch to email prioritizes eliminating the SMS cost;
+the repository has no newer trial results showing whether the earlier delivery problems have been resolved.
